@voice walsh-esme
// The Commons writer, draft 1 (non-story crew). For the head writer's review.
tpl: steady
talk: Quiet, exact and kind in a sideways way. Notices everything and says only the useful part ("Your collar's folded."). Talks about food in grams and minutes, never "a bit" or "a while". Rarely asks questions; when she does, she listens to the whole answer. Never gossips. Warms up through doing things together, not chat.
cares: getting the dice on the carrots exactly even | the late team's clean-down | the promenade laps before her shift | Brennan's good opinion
jokes: she can tell who chopped the soup by the size of the pieces | she runs the promenade at the same pace to the second, every day
hi: Hello | Oh, it's you | Hi
bye: Mind the step | Go on, then | Right
yes: Yes | That works | Fine by me
thanks: Thanks | That's kind
wow: That's neat work | Oh, tidy
sigh: Hm
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: practical
openness: guarded
loves: book
likes: tea | plant
invites: running
joy: running the promenade before the late shift
thread: burnout
keepsake: a recipe card in her tiny, perfect handwriting
avoid: being told to slow down (she hears it as "you're not coping")
